ed"]},"sid":["itu-9ead329e-331d-4056-9a41-7238df054a8a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Action Research Booklet","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747253","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We investigate three small employee-owned businesses: a consultancy, a business within art restoration, and a software business, and how they apply and reshape digital resources to commonly govern their businesses as there is no single tool that caters to their specific needs. Using the concept of digital bricolage as a lens, we find that the businesses apply a combination of digital resources at hand to meet their needs, they use these tools in well-known ways, and create new solutions, but do not look for ideal solutions. We furthermore find that believing in a common set of values shapes “the bricolage”, an aspect not found in the literature. These shared values further inform how technologies are used in practice. The values are shared internally but differ between the businesses. This has implications for the design of future tools that can help businesses govern collective decision-making.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776381"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design","Employee ownership"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing it for governance the case of employee owned businesses the case of employee owned businesses","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776381","identifier":[{"id":"85200656394","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2680c5af-21f5-4d28-a533-141becbc0080"],"keyword":["Design","Digital bricolage","Employee ownership"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17D899CE01AB1036901E7FBC7AD7EEDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-61698-3_2","issn":["03029743"],"pages":"13-26","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Interact 2023","title":"Design for Equality and Justice"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200656394"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2680c5af-21f5-4d28-a533-141becbc0080"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing IT for Governance - The Case of Employee-Owned Businesses. : The Case of Employee-Owned Businesses","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776381","year":"2024","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The cooperative model is known for its resilience and objective that prioritizes the common needs of their members, rather than returns for shareholders. The governance model follows a value-driven logic and a democratic structure, in that decision making is based on the “one person - one vote” principle. Under this umbrella, employee-owned businesses (EOBs) are organizations where the employees own and manage the company. Like other types of cooperatives, they arevalue driven, member owned, and democratically controlled organizations; principles that explain why EOBs have been economically sound and more resilient to crisis, such as Covid, compared to other types of organizations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Baka, Vasiliki","Nielsen, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718937"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cooperative","Cooperative governance","Digital era","employee owned businesses"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enacting cooperative governance in the digital era","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718937","ids":["itu-fd496beb-db0f-4958-93f1-7e992332a335"],"keyword":["Cooperative","cooperative governance","digital era","employee-owned businesses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D4A7CC146CC675D0349F2C2DE0EE63D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fd496beb-db0f-4958-93f1-7e992332a335"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enacting cooperative governance in the digital era","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718937","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The desire to create innovative organizational spaces has led to various instantiations of innovation ecosystems. Towards this direction, there is a growing interest in establishing corporate innovation ecosystems in the form of ‘corporate coworking spaces’ (CWS). From a relational ontological standpoint, this study builds on the collab- orative spaces literature with the aim to investigate the emerging dynamics between corporates and start-ups in an innovation ecosystem. Through an abductive research strategy (ARS) as well as service design methods, we explore how co-creation between corporates and start-ups emerges (or not) in an innovation ecosystem that serves as a collaborative space in Denmark. Our empirical findings challenge the mostly overenthusiastic con- notations and thus the study contributes to the critical coworking research stream. More specifically, we give emphasis on the co-constructive entanglement of socio-spatial arrangements and we propose a framework for revisiting the design of CWS through 1) balancing the engineered and evolving parts of the ecosystem, 2) facili- tating stakeholder alignment, 3) adopting a service-oriented approach and 4) developing inclusive strategies. Apart from the implications for scholars and practitioners who study and design CWS, we argue that future research would especially benefit from building on a service-oriented approach of innovation ecosystems and we call for more interdisciplinary research.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wagner, Sophia Aumüller","Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712563"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative spaces","Corporate coworking spaces","Innovation ecosystems","Open innovation","Service Design","Stakeholder alignment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"innovation ecosystems as a service exploring the dynamics between corporates amp start ups in the context of a corporate coworking space","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scaman.2023.101264","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712563","identifier":[{"id":"85149212385","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ef14b168-c00e-4d13-b263-7d0078a2bb07"],"keyword":["Collaborative spaces","Corporate coworking spaces","Innovation ecosystems","Open innovation","Service design","Stakeholder alignment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FAA1454CE0D6251F4BD587FC0251AA51"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0956522123000052/pdfft?md5=1032ff76cc8860c85ea49e2b1ff147df&pid=1-s2.0-S0956522123000052-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scaman.2023.101264","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sophia Aumüller","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, Sophia Aumüller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scaman.2023.101264","issn":["09565221","18733387"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Management","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Management","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149212385"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ef14b168-c00e-4d13-b263-7d0078a2bb07"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Innovation Ecosystems as a Service: : Exploring the Dynamics between Corporates &amp; Start-ups in the Context of a Corporate Coworking Space","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712563","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Udbredelsen og kendskabet til demokratiske virksomheder er begrænset både i det danske samfund, i undervisningssystemet og ikke mindst i rådgivningssystemet. De demokratiske virksomheder kan noget andet end de mere traditionelle virksomheder foruden, at de kan styrke iværksætteri. Det er derfor et problem, at rådgivning og uddannelse i demokratisk iværksætteri er fraværende eller begrænset. Der er således et stort potentiale i at fremme demokratiske virksomhedsformer og demokratisk iværksætteri, men opgaven i at styrke forståelsen og rådgivningen af demokratiske virksomheder er betragtelig. Hvis demokratisk iværksætteri skal tages alvorligt og blive en vigtig spiller samfundsmæssigt, som det er i andre EU-lande, skal det have større politisk bevågenhed og satsning, herunder introduceres i undervisningssystemet.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Victor, Fie Foged","Sivertsen, Stine","Baka, Vasiliki","Stana, Raluca Alexandra","Hansen, Anne Vorre","Riisgaard, Lone","Jakobsen, Gurli"],"cuid":["S02-097.13-038418"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"demokratisk iværksætteri erhvervsfremme og iværksætteri for demokratiske virksomheder i danmark sammenfatning","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/85229673/Demokratisk_Iv_rks_tteri.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.13-038418","ids":["itu-fd55a44d-95c3-4819-bf45-fc7d8cafa6ec","ruc-093741bc-4d76-47bd-98be-f01b3b26fea0"],"keyword":["Democratic Entrepreneurship"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","