{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383658"],"event":{"end":"2017-07-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2017-07-06","title":"European Group for Organizational Studies","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an enterprise social platform as a strategy tool in use to facilitate openness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383658","ids":["itu-a3d54235-0404-4955-9fdc-796ef2a94e9e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7B54EA8D90DDDA146C21399072177A0E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a3d54235-0404-4955-9fdc-796ef2a94e9e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An enterprise social platform as a strategy tool-in-use to facilitate openness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383658","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The automotive industry has proven to be a turbulent and complex environment where innovations occur as incremental product improvements, co-developed with external actors. Volvo Cars is one of the important multi-national players in the automotive market, creating world-changing innovation, and currently adapting to the increased connectivity by integrating over-the-air methods for distributing car software. The digital transformation has forced automotive manufacturers to rethink what creates value in today’s digital world and put the existing capabilities to the test. In this study, we explore the current challenges in the complex ecosystem of the automotive sector and how digital technology is perceived, introduced and adopted in a setting typical for the industry. Our results suggest that the management recognizes the vast potential from the increased connectivity, however adopting over-the-air software updatability is characterized by lack of sound business cases and unclear strategic direction. In order to meet the challenges, we consider it crucial that Volvo engages in the development of strong capabilities for integrating, building and reconfiguring its core competences while focusing on exploring external sources of digital innovation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Romanova, Gergana Petrova","Rosenmejer, Kasper","Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S02-081.24-038261"],"event":{"end":"2017-12-08","place":"San Francisco, us","start":"2017-12-07","title":"World Open Innovation Conference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"capabilities required for integrating external innovations within the automotive ecosystem a case study of volvo cars","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-081.24-038261","ids":["itu-187d32a0-70be-49b2-8667-513e598dedcd","ku-b4729880-6f46-4faf-b7d9-c136561d768d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-8999C0546ADEBCA2077FA6EADDC944D8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Production, Markets and Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Danske Bank A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Gergana Petrova","key":"romanovapau","last":"Romanova","locid":"8437e1c4-c361-457b-b644-fbc6348a9424","name":"Romanova, Gergana Petrova","orcid":"0000-0002-0524-7059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kasper","key":"rosenmejerpau","last":"Rosenmejer","name":"Rosenmejer, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","danske bank a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-187d32a0-70be-49b2-8667-513e598dedcd","ku-b4729880-6f46-4faf-b7d9-c136561d768d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Capabilities Required for Integrating External Innovations within the Automotive Ecosystem : A Case Study of Volvo Cars","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.24-038261","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The open mode of thinking, acting and being has been associated with liberating, participatory and collaborative arrangements that have prompted us to redefine how research, science, innovation and citizenship are to be conceived. In an era where much is said about the ‘open society’ and open innovation, looking at the interplay between involvement, technology and social good becomes of particular importance and interest. Having employed an action research approach, we examine how actors have enacted an open technology at the local governance level in a town in Zambia. Our interest is in how the different groups of local people have co-created the technology through multiple negotiations, organizational forms and institutional arrangements. Being theoretically inspired by the ‘technology enactment framework’, we propose an approach for framing the design of participatory technology projects at the local governance level, with implications for both theory and practice.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381384"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action research","Co creation","Developing country","Openness","Participatory governance","technology enactment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co creating an open platform at the local governance level how openness is enacted in zambia","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82933637/GIQ_D_15_00268R2.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381384","identifier":[{"id":"85005822603","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-08688847-6b6e-412b-b6a2-c7093df9310f"],"keyword":["Participatory governance","action research","co-creation","developing country","openness","technology enactment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22780C0E167DDED25FE534A75E0C8B2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82933637/GIQ_D_15_00268R2.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.giq.2016.10.001","issn":["0740624X","18729517"],"issn_org":["0740624X"],"journal":"Government Information Quarterly","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Government Information Quarterly"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85005822603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-08688847-6b6e-412b-b6a2-c7093df9310f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-creating an open platform at the local governance level: How openness is enacted in Zambia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381384","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki","Bogers, Marcel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-402709"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-16","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2016-12-15","title":"Annual World Open Innovation Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of transformational leaders in promoting open innovation the case of nasa space apps","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-402709","ids":["ku-0f9f4407-14c9-4f17-b236-3632d05166f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-66C455D46CEABBD510596F5F1399255A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Production, Markets and Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marcel","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"f9547890-2c59-4849-8168-b7f85890f431","name":"Bogers, Marcel","orcid":"0000-0002-7942-3561","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0f9f4407-14c9-4f17-b236-3632d05166f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The role of transformational leaders in promoting open innovation : the case of NASA Space Apps","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-402709","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In the last decade, we have witnessed an explosion of emergent web technologies and platforms that have drawn the attention of the academic community, as well as of professionals in many sectors. This paper explores the concept of reputation-making with the aim of explaining how the rise of user-generated content websites has influenced organizational reputation-making practices in the travel sector. The findings are based upon a corpus of data including: a field study at the offices of the largest travel user-generated website, TripAdvisor and an adaptation of virtual ethnography called ‘netnography’. In so doing, key insights are generated to inform organizational reputation-making. The paper concludes with the assertion that if we aim to understand the phenomenon of reputation-making, we have to develop a more nuanced and sophisticated way to conceptualize its formativeness. It is suggested that this extends beyond snap shot assessments or post hoc crisis management to an ongoing maintenance of the emergent and processual nature of reputation across the off-line and online spaces.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383389"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Process","Reputation management","Travel sector","User generated content"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formative reputation from being an organizational asset to becoming a process in the making","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82379250/CRR_Baka.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383389","identifier":[{"id":"84964575532","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-90089393-85c2-4893-80eb-2cbdf3ffa8b0"],"keyword":["process","reputation management","travel sector","user-generated content"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF7C0EA8DB49764836110B48DF9ED5A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82379250/CRR_Baka.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82379248/Baka.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1057/crr.2016.4","issn":["13633589","14791889"],"issn_org":["13633589"],"issue":"2","journal":"Corporate Reputation Review","pages":"152-165","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"Corporate Reputation Review","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964575532"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-90089393-85c2-4893-80eb-2cbdf3ffa8b0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formative Reputation: From Being an Organizational Asset to Becoming a Process in The Making","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383389","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381920"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"participatory citizen making in zambia an online intervention that matters international conference in urban property","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381920","ids":["itu-2c1f65a1-a530-460d-8912-5c43ad8239c6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F64AC83DC3C10597813DC2B2E4EDDC80"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2c1f65a1-a530-460d-8912-5c43ad8239c6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Participatory citizen making in Zambia: An (online) intervention that matters\", International Conference in Urban Property","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381920","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The paper explores how valuing devices and verification mechanisms such as user-generated content (UGC) websites partake in performing placeness. The findings are based upon a corpus of data including a case study at the offices of the largest user-generated travel website, TripAdvisor, a longitudinal netnographic approach and a conceptual review. Originally inspired by theorists of space we treat places as sites of becoming that are performed through everyday practices. In claiming that places become meaningful only in and through practices we stress the importance of treating rating and ranking mechanisms as generative, rather than merely reductive algorithmically produced representations. By juxtaposing traditional enactments of traveling, we are discussing how placeness has been transformed and how this has fueled a series of further revisions to valuing tourism. We conclude the paper by appreciating the multiplicity of performativity as being implicated in the algorithmic configurations on contemporary valuing devices and enacted as we read, interpret, write, imagine. It is suggested that although earlier valuing devices have evoked place-making in various ways, the rise of UGC websites has converted the travel experience into a constant negotiation process whereby both the value of places and the value of valuing devices are contested.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383134"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Performativity","Place making","Ranking","Rating","tourism practices","valuing devices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding valuing devices in tourism through place making","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80633964/VS.2001_5592.1532149_Baka.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383134","ids":["itu-7fdfc64f-2aca-4598-96ae-c2a838a5bf57"],"keyword":["Place-making","performativity","ranking","rating","tourism practices","valuing devices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C515AA09BE937DA75A6C5385818D86C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80633964/VS.2001_5592.1532149_Baka.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/vs.2001-5992.1532149","issn":["20015992"],"issue":"2","journal":"Valuation Studies","pages":"149-180","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","title":"Valuation Studies","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7fdfc64f-2aca-4598-96ae-c2a838a5bf57"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Understanding valuing devices in tourism through ‘place-making’","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383134","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The emergence of User-Generated-Content (UGC) is challenging the equilibrium of reputation management practices prompting widespread change and organizational restructuring. Formal accreditation schemes mingle with less formal mechanisms which place users in the middle making them draw their own conclusions about products and services. This paper explores how UGC reviews and ratings have intensified the contingency of organizational reputation in the travel sector. The findings are based upon a corpus of data including: a field study at the offices of the largest travel user-generated website, TripAdvisor, and a netnographic approach. In particular we discuss the shift from Word-Of-Mouth to eWOM, the consequences for the sector and provide a balanced view of the role of reviews, ratings and lists. We are concluding with a conceptual model for managing online reputation in the era of UGC, while acknowledging the current process of transformation in reputation management","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384083"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Rankings","Reputation management","Reviews","User generated content","eWOM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the becoming of user generated reviews looking at the past to understand the future of managing reputation in the travel sector","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825256/JTMA_D_14_00885R1_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384083","identifier":[{"id":"84944203227","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c0e6cd1b-0f54-4303-ad88-580abb79c49a"],"keyword":["User-Generated-Content","eWOM","rankings","reputation management","reviews"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA2197E78E9DB506EB8D37AC9AFBFEA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825256/JTMA_D_14_00885R1_1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tourman.2015.09.004","issn":["02615177","18793193"],"issn_org":["02615177"],"journal":"Tourism Management","pages":"148-162","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Tourism Management","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944203227"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c0e6cd1b-0f54-4303-ad88-580abb79c49a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The becoming of user-generated reviews: Looking at the past to understand the future of managing reputation in the travel sector","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384083","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this paper is to explore how a technological platform can connect multiple stakeholders towards educating open innovation ambassadors. In other words, how both academics and practitioners focusing on open innovation can ‘meet’ to constructively nurture openness in practice. The paper presents an exploratory case study of how a technological platform has served as the place where meaningful interactions among students, academics and practitioners of open innovation emerged with interesting insights for all. The themes that emerged revolve around the notions of affordances, boundaries, co-creation, interactivity and wholeness. The study contributes a discussion about how openness can be enacted in theoretical institutions and organizational contexts and offers possible avenues through which to build a bridge among all stakeholders.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384038"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co creation","Interactivity","Open innovation","Stakeholder engagement","Technological Platform"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"practicing theory and theorizing practice using an open collaborative platform to facilitate meaningful interactions between academia and industry","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384038","ids":["itu-bd84b0c2-af57-4f3b-9a07-5fc648213591"],"keyword":["Co-creation","Interactivity","Open Innovation","Stakeholder Engagement","Technological Platform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E4AF65F85BD214F2EF8C77E0A8B650BE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bd84b0c2-af57-4f3b-9a07-5fc648213591"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Practicing theory and theorizing practice: Using an Open Collaborative Platform to facilitate meaningful interactions between academia and industry","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384038","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In the ever-evolving organizational environment where the only constant is change, there is an increasing need to revisit the interrelationships between organizational routines and change. From a practice lens perspective, routines are treated as generative systems created through the interplays between actions people undertake and the patterns and structures these actions in turn recreate. Although the seminal work on routines as practices has acknowledged their dynamism, there is yet a long way to go until we fully understand and exemplify the relationships between organizational routines and change, as well as how and why technological evolution has transformed organizational routines into generative systems. How are routines to be perceived if as Chia (2002) more strongly puts it, all we have is change? Inspired by how process theorists have analyzed change, the paper draws on this work to discuss how reputation-making routines have changed in the travel sector. The primary research question focuses on how reputation-making routines become over time and what the role of algorithmic classification systems in this process is. By closely studying reputation-making routines we propose a reconceptualization of change, as constant transformation rather than aberration of sameness or stability and we gain a more insightful understanding of the interplays between the ways routines are enacted on a micro level.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730201"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Algorithmic classification","Change management","Generative systems","Micro level enactment","Organizational routines","Practice lens","Process theory","Reputation making routines","Technological evolution","Travel sector"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the becoming of reputation making routines bridging the practice lens with process studies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-730201","ids":["itu-eec49781-e8ca-4834-a375-3d1fd6e18cee"],"keyword":["Algorithmic classification","Change management","Generative systems","Micro-level enactment","Organizational routines","Practice lens","Process theory","Reputation-making routines","Technological evolution","Travel sector"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-39E9D62F5DD374147F850B4403D6DB8E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-eec49781-e8ca-4834-a375-3d1fd6e18cee"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Becoming of Reputation-making Routines: Bridging the Practice Lens with Process Studies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730201","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Increasing use of collaborative technologies has transformed organizational dynamics in novel ways. In this paper, we adopt the principle of wholeness in designing an integrated open innovation system. We provide an overview of existing collaborative technologies and situate the proposed sociotechnical arrangement within the paradigm of open innovation. We explore how effectively technological platforms address emergent collaboration and innovation practices within and across organizations and to which extent existing technologies act as strategic catalysts of open innovation. We argue that in embracing wholeness and in treating technologies as inseparable constitutive parts of organizational architecture, we foster organizational and institutional collaboration and encourage innovative practices. The focus of the paper is on how the design of sociotechnical systems as wholes, that is systems that are concurrently acting as corporate websites, internal collaboration spaces, extranets and social media aggregators, actively promotes open innovation in practice. We close with a presentation of six cases that are illustrative of how such a system could be applicable within the open innovation paradigm, namely, citizen participation, crowdsourcing and open innovation contests, open source innovation, reviews and social media, social enterprises and open teaching.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Baka, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383462"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative technologies","Open Innovation System","Organizational Wholeness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing an integrated open innovation system towards organizational wholeness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2641580.2641595","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383462","identifier":[{"id":"84908622033","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-95807fbc-2a9c-4ef5-b54b-339f3c72d579"],"keyword":["Collaborative Technologies","Open Innovation System","Organizational Wholeness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF9176A84D143D87D9DC691665DB2DC9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2641580.2641595","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2641595","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"bakapau","last":"Baka","locid":"4e33d926-364b-47b8-97d7-409c16b62db9","name":"Baka, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0001-7738-7846","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2641580.2641595","eisbn":["9781450330169"],"series":"Proceedings of The International Symposium on Open Collaboration","status":"p","title":"OpenSym '14 Proceedings of The International Symposium on Open Collaboration"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84908622033"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-95807fbc-2a9c-4ef5-b54b-339f3c72d579"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DESIGNING AN INTEGRATED OPEN INNOVATION SYSTEM: TOWARDS ORGANIZATIONAL WHOLENESS","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383462","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
